---
layout: base.njk
comments: true
commentsCategory: episodes
---
<article class="chapter" data-chapter-id="{{ id }}">
  <header class="chapter-header">
    <nav class="chapter-breadcrumb" aria-label="Chapter location" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <ol class="breadcrumb" role="list">
        <li><a href="/star-rangers/seasons/">Seasons</a></li>
        <li><a href="/star-rangers/seasons/s{{ season | zeroPad }}/">{{ season | seasonLabel }}</a></li>
        <li><a href="/star-rangers/seasons/s{{ season | zeroPad }}/e{{ episode | zeroPad }}/">Episode {{ episode }}</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">Chapter {{ chapter }}</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="chapter-meta">
      <span class="chapter-label">S{{ season | zeroPad }}E{{ episode | zeroPad }}C{{ chapter | zeroPad }}</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="chapter-title">{{ title }}</h1>

    <dl class="chapter-details">
      {% if timestamp %}
      <div class="chapter-detail">
        <dt>Time</dt>
        <dd>{{ timestamp }}</dd>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if location %}
      <div class="chapter-detail">
        <dt>Location</dt>
        <dd>{{ location }}</dd>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </dl>

    {% if tags and tags.length %}
    <ul class="chapter-tags" aria-label="Tags" role="list">
      {% for tag in tags %}
      <li class="chapter-tag">{{ tag }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}

    {#- Optional, and no chapter has one yet - the field exists so a chapter
        can carry its own Open Graph preview instead of falling back to the
        site hero (see OG_IMAGE_DIRS in .eleventy.js). Rendered here on the
        same pattern as lore-entry.njk / codex.njk so the file a card shows is
        the file a reader sees, rather than a preview-only asset nobody on the
        page can check against its own alt text. -#}
    {% if image %}
    <img class="entry-image" src="/star-rangers/images/chapters/{{ image }}" alt="{{ image_alt | default(title) }}" />
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  {%- set visiblePovs = povs | povsForTier -%}
  {% if visiblePovs and visiblePovs.length %}
  <div class="pov-controls" role="group" aria-label="Point of view selector">
    <p class="pov-controls__label">View from:</p>
    <div class="pov-controls__buttons">
      <button
        class="pov-btn pov-btn--all pov-btn--active"
        data-pov="all"
        aria-pressed="true"
        type="button"
      >All POVs</button>
      {% for pov in visiblePovs %}
      <button
        class="pov-btn"
        data-pov="{{ pov.id }}"
        aria-pressed="false"
        type="button"
      >{{ pov.label }}</button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {#- "From the Archive": the Archive entries that accompany this chapter -
      pages whose revealed_by names it, plus the chapter's own `related:`
      titles - each with the entry's own one-line account, in the Archive's
      voice (lib/archive-companions.js; Dermot's direction of 2026-10-05, the
      Archive as the Book that accompanies the narrative). Where it sits is
      the posture's: beside the prose in the archive and contemplative
      presentations at the wide breakpoint, under it in story and primer
      (main.css, .chapter-reading). The DOM order is the same either way, so
      a reader without the grid meets it directly under the text. -#}
  {%- set archiveCompanions = { id: id } | fromTheArchive(related, collections.glossary, collections.lore, collections.codex, edition.tier) -%}
  <div class="chapter-reading">
  <div class="chapter-body">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>
  {% if archiveCompanions.length %}
  <aside class="archive-companions" aria-labelledby="archive-companions-heading" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <h2 class="archive-companions__heading" id="archive-companions-heading">From the Archive</h2>
    <p class="archive-companions__lede">The record's entries for what this chapter meets.</p>
    <ul class="archive-companions__list" role="list">
      {% for entry in archiveCompanions %}
      <li class="archive-companions__item">
        <a class="archive-companions__title" href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.title }}</a>
        <span class="archive-companions__kind">{{ entry.label }}{% if entry.category %} · {{ entry.category }}{% endif %}{% if entry.relation == "revealed" %} · first revealed here{% endif %}</span>
        {% if entry.text %}<p class="archive-companions__text">{{ entry.text }}</p>{% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </aside>
  {% endif %}
  </div>

  {% set scenes = scenePovPages | scenesForChapter(id) %}
  {% if scenes.length %}
  <section class="chapter-scenes" aria-label="Scenes in this chapter" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <h2 class="chapter-scenes__heading">Read scene-by-scene</h2>
    {% for scene in scenes %}
    <div class="chapter-scene">
      <p class="chapter-scene__label">Scene {{ scene.number }}</p>
      <ul class="chapter-scene__povs" role="list">
        {% for entry in scene.characters %}
        <li><a href="/star-rangers{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.character.label }}</a></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if canon_facts and canon_facts.length %}
  <aside class="canon-facts" aria-label="Verified canon facts for this chapter">
    <h2 class="canon-facts__heading">
      <button class="canon-facts__toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="canon-facts-list" type="button">
        Canon Facts <span aria-hidden="true">▸</span>
      </button>
    </h2>
    <ul class="canon-facts__list" id="canon-facts-list" hidden>
      {% for fact in canon_facts %}
      <li>{{ fact }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </aside>
  {% endif %}

  {#- "In the Archive": the record's own pages that read this chapter, derived
      at build time (lib/archive-backlinks.js) from the included lore,
      glossary, codex and journal collections. Kept after the prose and the
      canon facts on purpose: the general tier is "the same record with its
      reasons under it", and the reasons go under the text, not beside it. -#}
  {%- set archiveLinks = { id: id, comment_id: comment_id } | archiveBacklinks(collections.lore, collections.glossary, collections.codex, collections.journalEntries) -%}
  {% if archiveLinks.length %}
  <aside class="archive-links" aria-labelledby="archive-links-heading" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <h2 class="archive-links__heading" id="archive-links-heading">In the Archive</h2>
    <p class="archive-links__lede">Pages of the record that read this chapter.</p>
    <ul class="archive-links__list" role="list">
      {% for link in archiveLinks %}
      <li>
        <a href="/star-rangers{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a>
        <span class="archive-links__kind">{{ link.label }}{% if link.relation == "revealed" %} · first revealed here{% elif link.relation == "revised" %} · revised after this chapter{% endif %}</span>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </aside>
  {% endif %}

  {% set previousChapter = collections.chapters | previousChapterIn(id) %}
  {% set nextChapter = collections.chapters | nextChapterIn(id) %}
  <nav class="chapter-pagination" aria-label="Chapter navigation" data-pagefind-ignore>
    {% if previousChapter %}
    <a class="chapter-pagination__prev" href="/star-rangers{{ previousChapter.url }}">
      ← {{ previousChapter.data.title }}
    </a>
    {% endif %}
    {% if nextChapter %}
    <a class="chapter-pagination__next" href="/star-rangers{{ nextChapter.url }}">
      {{ nextChapter.data.title }} →
    </a>
    {% endif %}
  </nav>

  {#- Surfaces the permanent citation alias (src/chapter-aliases.njk). Without
      this the aliases exist and nobody knows, which is no use to the wiki
      editor or blogger they were built for. Deliberately says WHY the address
      differs from the one in the address bar - "permanent link" alone invites
      the reasonable assumption that the visible URL is already permanent, and
      it is not: renumbering reassigns a chapter's URL to different content.
      data-pagefind-ignore because 35 copies of the same sentence would
      otherwise crowd search results. -#}
  {% if comment_id %}
  <p class="chapter-permalink" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <strong>Citing this chapter?</strong> Use
    <a href="/star-rangers/c/{{ comment_id }}/"><code>/c/{{ comment_id }}/</code></a>.
    Chapters get renumbered as the story's chronology settles, which changes the
    address above — this one follows the chapter instead of the slot, so it stays
    pointing at these words.
  </p>
  {% endif %}
</article>
